# Working screenshots. Only the four assets package.json and README reference
# are tracked; the rest stay local. Same allow-list shape as .vscodeignore.
media/*
!media/icon.png
!media/screenshot-deck.png
!media/screenshot-topology.png
!media/screenshot-inspector.png

# The whole .claude/ directory: agent definitions, skills, working notes and
# settings.local.json. Local tooling, not product. Untracked before the public
# flip - untracking is reversible, publishing is not.
.claude/

# OpenCode's per-project state directory: opencode.json, its own node_modules,
# package files. Local tooling of the engine this repo now observes - same
# treatment as .claude/. The AGENTS.md context file at the repo root is NOT
# covered by this rule: whether it is tracked is a deliberate open decision.
.opencode/

# --- The maintainer's private half (ported from release/0.5.0, 2026-08-28) ---
#
# `lab/` is the private repository holding the working method, the evidence, the
# unredacted captures and the identity set. It is OPTIONAL: nothing here depends
# on it, the suite is green without it, and `scripts/privacy-sweep.mjs` reports
# `identity=SKIPPED` rather than failing when it is absent.
#
# It was NOT ignored on this branch, and that is why this block exists. A single
# `git add -A` here would have committed `lab/identity.local.json` - the token
# set the whole scrub was run to remove - into the repository the scrub had just
# cleaned and pushed.
lab/

# The working method and its evidence, presented back at these paths by links
# into `lab/` so `/phase` and `/handoff` still resolve them locally while
# nothing here tracks a byte of them. `docs/` and `spike/` are directory
# junctions; the five files are SYMLINKS, not hardlinks - measured 2026-08-28,
# a rename-based write (`sed -i`, and most editors) severs a hardlink and
# replaces a symlink with a regular file, leaving a detached copy at this root
# that looks correct and never reaches `lab/`. Write these paths in place.
#
# ANCHORED WITH A LEADING SLASH, every one of them. `docs/` unanchored would
# also ignore a future `src/docs/`, and `CLAUDE.md` unanchored would ignore one
# at any depth.
/CLAUDE.md
/PLAN.md
/HANDOVER.md
/AGENTS.md
/agent-deck-spec.md
/docs/
/spike/
